  "title": "Key signatures",
  "summary": "Each key has its own set of sharps or flats, written once at the start of the music.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Key signature",
      "body": "Instead of writing ♯ or ♭ next to every note, written music lists the sharps or flats of the key once, at the start. That list is the **key signature**. G major's key signature is one sharp, F♯. F major's is one flat, B♭. C major's is empty.\n\n**Why it matters:** The number of sharps or flats tells you the key at a glance. On a chart, two sharps means the notes of D major.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        66,
        70
      ],
      "labels": {
        "66": "F♯: G major",
        "70": "B♭: F major"
      }
    },
